            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દાઢ — dāḍh — \"molar, back tooth\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "મારી દાઢ હવે નથી દુખતી. — mārī dāḍh have nathī dukhtī — \"My back tooth doesn't hurt any more.\""
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Not દાઢી, a beard."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "દાઢ (dāḍh) is a tadbhava. It comes from dāṁṣṭra, \"fang, tusk\", beside Sanskrit daṁṣṭra, \"tusk, fang\"; CDIAL glosses the Gujarati word \"molar\" (CDIAL 6250)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
